        const PASSAGE_TRIP = `How to Plan and Save for a Budget-Friendly Trip\n\nTraveling can be a great way for young people to take a break from their busy routines and to experience new places. However, enjoyable trip might be too expensive for most of them. With careful planning and regular saving, you can prepare for a vacation that does not cost too much money. The following steps help you plan a trip that fits your budget.\n\n1. Set a Travel Goal\nFirst, decide where you want to go, how long you will stay, and what you want to do there. A clear goal makes it easier to estimate how much money you need. For example, a three-day trip to a nearby city will usually cost less than a week-long international trip.\n\n2. Make a Budget Plan\nNext, list the main expenses you expect, including transportation, accommodation, food, entrance fees, and activities. For example, if you plan to visit several attractions, check their entrance fees before deciding how much money to prepare. A detailed budget helps you avoid unnecessary spending.\n\n3. Prepare an Emergency Fund\nSet aside extra money for unexpected situations. A delayed trip, lost belongings, or an urgent need may require additional expenses. Keeping about 10 percent of your travel budget as an emergency fund can provide extra protection.\n\n4. Find Ways to Reduce Costs\nLook for affordable options before making bookings. Compare prices for transportation and accommodation, check discounts, and consider traveling during less busy periods. You can also choose free or low-cost activities, such as visiting public parks or local markets.\n\n5. Set a Savings Target\nFinally, calculate how much you need to save each month before your travel. For example, if you need Rp3,000,000 in six months, you can set aside about Rp500,000 each month. Record your savings regularly and reduce unnecessary spending if you are falling behind.`;

